# Feature-branch workflow

When the user asks for code or project changes in this repo, do not work on `master` (or `main`). This repo opts in to commit, push, and auto-merge on feature branches without a separate "please commit" or "please merge" request.

## Before editing
1. If HEAD is `master`/`main`, create and check out a new branch named `cursor/<short-kebab-description>`.
2. If already on a feature branch that matches this request, keep using it.
3. Call SetActiveBranch after creating or switching branches.
4. Stage only files from this request. Leave unrelated dirty files (and secrets) unstaged.

## After the change is done
1. Commit the relevant files with a concise message focused on why.
2. Push the feature branch: `git push -u origin HEAD`.
3. Open a PR and merge it immediately (`gh pr create`, then `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch`). Do not wait for the user to test first.
4. If this session is on the local PC (not a cloud agent VM), check out `master`/`main` and `git pull` so the local tree matches the merge.
5. Tell the user the branch name, PR URL, and that it is merged.

## Never
- Do not `git push` to `master` or `main` (merge via GitHub PR only).
- Do not leave a completed task unmerged on a feature branch.
- Do not force-push, skip hooks, or amend unless the user explicitly asks.
